::SPEECH_U04_L04_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U04_L04_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.RES.04
Question:
Source excerpt for item 1: A speaker uses source details to make a careful inference for a research-supported presentation. Which choice best shows supported inference skill?
{
~A. Make a guess with no source support#This answer shows a misconception. Return to the source details and check whether the choice supports accurate research-based speaking.
~B. Repeat one word from the source without reasoning#This answer is not strong enough because it does not connect source understanding to the speech purpose and audience need.
=C. Base the inference on direct details from the source#Correct. This answer uses the source accurately and connects the information to research-supported speech communication.
~D. Ignore the direct details in the source#This answer weakens communication by relying on a surface detail instead of accurate source comprehension.
}
::SPEECH_U04_L04_Quiz_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U04_L04_Quiz_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.RES.03
Question:
Source excerpt for item 2: A speaker uses source details to make a careful inference for a research-supported presentation. Which choice best shows supported inference skill?
{
=A. Explain how the source detail supports the conclusion#Correct. This answer uses the source accurately and connects the information to research-supported speech communication.
~B. Repeat one word from the source without reasoning#This answer is not strong enough because it does not connect source understanding to the speech purpose and audience need.
~C. Claim the source proves every possible outcome#This answer may mention the topic, but it does not show the careful reading or reasoning required for source use.
~D. Ignore the direct details in the source#This answer weakens communication by relying on a surface detail instead of accurate source comprehension.
}
